title: Genesis 11 – The Spirit of Babylon
description: A study from Genesis 11: Babel as the first one-world, works-based religion, spiritual whoredom against a jealous God, and the whore of Babylon at the end.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-11-spirit-of-babylon.html

=== Introduction
--- The Spirit of Babylon [title]
overline: A study from Genesis 11
sub: Works religion as spiritual whoredom, from the tower of Babel to the whore of Babylon.
refs: Genesis 11:4; Revelation 17:5
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

--- The context
lead: The study of Revelation 17, the whore of Babylon and the fall of that wicked city, has a lot of context coming from scripture.
- The faithfulness of God.
- The betrothal to His people.
- The eventual marriage of the Lamb. [[Revelation 19:7-9]]
center: There are many chapters and verses on this. These should give you some ideas of this major theme throughout the Bible.

=== A jealous God
--- Whose name is Jealous
scripture: Exodus 34:12-17 | mark: the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God; go a whoring after their gods
p: God has given us His law regarding marriage as a picture of His relationship with the saved. He is a jealous God. He speaks against idolatry and having other gods, the blasphemy of worshipping graven and molten images or other creatures in His stead, as fornication. Whoredoms. Harlotry.
refs: Exodus 34:6-7

--- The spirit of jealousy
scripture: Numbers 5:30 | mark: the spirit of jealousy
scripture: Deuteronomy 23:17
p: He draws a parallel to actual whores: allowing the daughters of your land to commit fornication destroys a nation, as destruction is visited on those who forsake Him to chase after strange gods.

=== Jerusalem the harlot
--- Thy birth is of the land of Canaan
scripture: Ezekiel 16:2-6 | mark: Live
kicker: Ezekiel 16
p: God found her cast out in the open field, polluted in her own blood, and said unto her, Live.

--- Thou becamest mine
scripture: Ezekiel 16:8-14 | mark: entered into a covenant with thee, saith the Lord GOD, and thou becamest mine
center: The covenant, the washing, the clothing and the crown: all His comeliness, which He put upon her.

--- But thou didst trust in thine own beauty
scripture: Ezekiel 16:15-17 | mark: thou didst trust in thine own beauty, and playedst the harlot
panel-warn: Images of men | Taking His gold and silver to make idols. [[Ezekiel 16:17]]
panel-warn: Her children | Sacrificing the sons and daughters born unto Him. [[Ezekiel 16:20-21]]
refs: Ezekiel 16:18-22

--- As a wife that committeth adultery
scripture: Ezekiel 16:30-34 | mark: as a wife that committeth adultery, which taketh strangers instead of her husband
refs: Ezekiel 16:26-29

--- Judged as women that break wedlock
scripture: Ezekiel 16:35-38 | mark: I will judge thee, as women that break wedlock
refs: Ezekiel 16:39-43

--- Thy sister Sodom
scripture: Ezekiel 16:46-50 | mark: pride, fulness of bread, and abundance of idleness
refs: Ezekiel 16:51-52

--- Yet I will remember my covenant
scripture: Ezekiel 16:59-63 | mark: I will remember my covenant with thee in the days of thy youth
center: “I will establish unto thee an everlasting covenant.”

=== The spirit of Babel
--- Adultery, fornication, whoredoms
lead: The spirit of Babel, which is Babylon, and the empires and kingdoms that followed it, is one of adultery. Fornication. Whoredoms.
big: Genesis 11:4 | mark: let us build us a city and a tower, whose top may reach unto heaven; and let us make us a name
p: The original sin of the first one-world religion and government, just years after the flood, was to blaspheme God by building a tower to Heaven. Working their way to righteousness, that they may become as gods. [[Genesis 3:5]] [[lesson:genesis-11-tower-of-babel|The Tower of Babel]]

--- A symbol of all works religion
panel: The Tower of Babel | A symbol of all works-based false religion. Its destruction, a picture of the end times.
panel: Babylon the empire | Nebuchadnezzar and his idol, a picture of the beast and his abomination. [[Daniel 3:1-6]] [[Revelation 13:14-15]]
callout: This spirit of Babylon and its whore of self-righteous works religion, bowing to idols, worshipping the created more than the Creator, is fornication. Harlots, taking from God what is His, leading man to fornication. [[Romans 1:25]]

--- Mystery, Babylon the Great
big: Revelation 17:5 | mark: MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS
refs: Revelation 17:1-2; Revelation 18:2-4

=== Put away for fornication
--- Except it be for fornication
big: Matthew 19:9 | mark: except it be for fornication
p: God’s law says that a betrothed groom can only put away his intended bride for fornication. And no man may then marry her that has been put away.
note: This is the context, fulfilled in the end times prophecy. [[lesson:pulled-israel-put-away|Israel Put Away]]

--- The Bride, the Lamb’s wife
big: Revelation 19:7-8 | mark: the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready
refs: Revelation 21:9; 2 Corinthians 11:2

=== Close
--- Come out of her [title]
overline: Genesis 11 and Revelation 17
point: A jealous God | He calls idolatry and works religion what it is: whoredom.
point: Babel to Babylon | The tower was the first one-world, works-based false religion, and its fall pictures the end.
point: The Bride | Kept for the Lamb, espoused as a chaste virgin to Christ. [[2 Corinthians 11:2]]
point: Come out of her, my people | That ye be not partakers of her sins. [[Revelation 18:4]]

